"<strong>Setups in the demo:</strong> this worksheet uses Lens in white light and Mirror in white light. The other setups (Converging lens, Magnifier, Camera, Concave mirror, Telescope, Prism, Total internal reflection, Microscope, Refracting surface, Apparent depth) belong to other worksheets.",
"A parallel beam of white light, like the light from a distant star, falls on a lens or a curved mirror. The rays are traced as they bend or bounce. Where they cross is the <strong>focus</strong>.",
"White light is split into seven colors from violet ({#} nm) to red ({#} nm), each traced on its own. The small “on the screen” picture shows the spot the light makes on the screen.",
